  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 218 PM MDT THU OCT 1 2026\nThe trend of warmer and drier than normal is set to continue\nthrough the period, with temperatures staying 10 to 15 degrees \nabove normal. Sunday is forecast to be the warmest day with the \nfurthest north amplification of the upper-level ridge over the \narea and southerly flow aloft. Temperatures are forecast to be \nnear record highs for the day across the region. On Monday, a \nweak upper-level shortwave trough will move through the area, \nsuppressing the ridge further south. This system will increase \ncloud cover and support a low chance (5-10%) of showers near the\nNV border and south-central Idaho mountains. Temperatures will \ncool by a couple of degrees Mon/Tue, before the upper ridge \nrebounds and warm and dry conditions prevail.",
